UID:9a357b4f58fdb4a3@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260817T130341Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260805
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Cancellation of Certificate of Title for Tiny
  Home and Manufactured Home
DESCRIPTION:Important Information Regarding Cancellation of Certificate of
  Title:\nPursuant to\nTitle 29-A\, section §669\n\, beginning on July 29\
 , 2026\, residents of the state of Maine are able to request cancellation 
 of their Certificate of Title for Tiny Home or Manufactured Home for purpo
 ses of obtaining residential real property.\nWhen a Tiny Home or Manufactu
 red Home is\npermanently affixed to land that you own\, or land where you 
 have permission from the land owner via a signed sworn statement\n\, you m
 ay request to cancel the Certificate of Title. Once the Certificate of Tit
 le is cancelled\, the home becomes part of the residential real property i
 nstead of being treated as personal property. Under Maine law\, this proce
 ss is handled through the county Registry of Deeds and the Maine Secretary
  of State Bureau of Motor Vehicles.\nHow to Cancel your Certificate of Tit
 tle for Tiny Home or Manufactured Home\nBefore requesting cancellation of 
 the title\, make sure:\nYou own both the manufactured home or tiny home\na
 nd\nthe land where it is located\;\nand/or\nThe individual that owns the p
 roperty has given a sworn signed statement of authorization.\nThe home has
  been\npermanently affixed\nto the property in accordance with Maine law.\
 nAny existing liens have been released or the lienholder has agreed to rel
 ease the lien upon cancellation of the title.\nThis process is not for dou
 ble-wide mobile homes/trailers\n1. Gather the required documentation\nYou 
 will need to obtain the following documents before submitting your request
 :\nThe Original Certificate of Title\nA description of the home\, includin
 g\;\nModel Year\nManufacturer {make}\nWidth\nLength\nIdentification Number
 /Serial Number\nLien Release Documentation\,\nif applicable\nThe legal des
 cription of the real property\nA sworn statement confirming:\nYou own both
  the land\, and the Tiny Home or Manufactured Home\, or a sworn statement 
 from the property land owner\nThe home is permanently affixed to the prope
 rty/ground\nIf you are unable to locate your current Certificate\nhttps://
 www.maine.gov/sos/bmv/vehicles/titles/tiny-and-manufactured-homes-conversi
 on-to-real-property
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/bmv/vehicles/titles/tiny-and-manufactured-ho
 mes-conversion-to-real-property
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:797380b6c62afe21@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260817T130341Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260804
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Tiny Home and Manufactured Home Information
DESCRIPTION:Important Information Regarding Cancellation of Certificate of
  Title:\nPursuant to\nTitle 29-A\, section §669\n\, beginning on July 29\
 , 2026\, residents of the state of Maine are able to request cancellation 
 of their Certificate of Title for Tiny Home or Manufactured Home for purpo
 ses of obtaining residential real property.\nIf you are interested in the 
 process of cancelling your current Certificate of Title\, check out some o
 f the links below before continuing.\nThis webpage provides general inform
 ation about Tiny Homes and Manufactured Homes\, with a focus on the titlin
 g process requirements and related regulations\, as well as the cancellati
 on of Certificate of Title for purposes of obtaining residential real prop
 erty. It is designed to help homeowners\, buyers\, sellers\, and the publi
 c better understand how Tiny Homes and Manufactured Homes are classified\,
  when a title is required\, and the processes involved in obtaining\, tran
 sferring\, or updating a title. The information presented is intended as a
 n educational resource based on Maine's applicable guidelines and requirem
 ents. Visitors can explore common questions\, learn about titling procedur
 es\, and find helpful explanations to better navigate the ownership and re
 gistration process for Tiny Homes and Manufactured Homes in Maine.\nHere a
 re some quick reference links\, you may need these before continuing:\nCon
 version to Real Property Process\nMaine State Revised Statues Website\nPro
 perty Definitions\nThis section provides information to help homeowners\, 
 buyers\, and other interested parties understand the types of construction
 \, material\, and installation that classify each type of home. By outlini
 ng these definitions. Read through the below definitions for the appropria
 te boxes to get more information.\nTiny Home Definition\nPursuant to Maine
  Statute\n29-A\, section §101\, subsection 80-C\n\, Maine's definition of
  a "Tiny Home" is a living space permanently constructed on a frame or cha
 ssis and designed for use as permanent living quarters\nhttps://www.maine.
 gov/sos/bmv/vehicles/titles/tiny-and-manufactured-homes
URL:https://www.maine.gov/sos/bmv/vehicles/titles/tiny-and-manufactured-ho
 mes
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
