UID:92cca0d2b9b26244@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260813T024414Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Title IV Postsecondary Institutions: Workforc
 e Pell Program Application Now Open
DESCRIPTION:Skip First Level Navigation\nSkip All Navigation\nMaine.gov\nA
 gencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Maine.gov\nMaine Departmen
 t of Labor\nContact Us\n|\nNews\n|\nOnline services\n|\nPublications\n|\nS
 itemap\nHome\nContact Us\nOnline Services\nAbout MDOL\nNews & Events\nForm
 s & Publications\nMDOL Bureaus\nHome\n→\nNews & Events\n→ Title IV Pos
 tsecondary Institutions: Workforce Pell Program Application Now Open\nServ
 ices\nJobs & Training\nUnemployment Insurance\nDisability Services\nWorkpl
 ace Safety\nLabor Laws\nLabor Statistics\nWorkforce Development\nTitle IV 
 Postsecondary Institutions: Workforce Pell Program Application Now Open\nA
 ugust 12\, 2026\nFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE: August 12\, 2026\nTitle IV Postsec
 ondary Institutions: Workforce Pell Program Application Now Open\nMAINE-\n
 The State Workforce Development Board (SWDB) -\nhttps://www.maine.gov/swb/
 board/index.shtml\nannounced the launch of Maine's Workforce Pell Applicat
 ion -\nhttps://www.worksourcemaine.com/pages/workforce-pell\n\, providing 
 eligible Title IV postsecondary institutions with an online process to see
 k approval to offer Workforce Pell-eligible programs.\nThe launch of the a
 pplication follows the U.S. Department of Education's publication of the f
 inal Workforce Pell regulations -\nhttps://www.ed.gov/about/news/press-rel
 ease/us-department-of-education-issues-final-rule-create-new-workforce-pel
 l-grant-program\n(effective July 20\, 2026). Workforce Pell expands federa
 l Pell Grant eligibility to approved short-term workforce training program
 s that prepare students for high-skill\, high-wage\, and in-demand careers
 . Under Workforce Pell\, states are responsible for reviewing and certifyi
 ng eligible programs before approval by the U.S. Department of Education.\
 n"Workforce Pell opens the door to new education and career opportunities 
 for more people across our state\,"\nsaid Vaughan Woodruff\, Chair\, State
  Workforce Development Board\n. "The Maine Workforce Pell program makes it
  easier for individuals to access those opportunities\, strengthening the 
 futures o\nhttp://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=1335766
 8
URL:http://www.maine.gov/labor/news_events/article.shtml?id=13357668
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:e80469cb8aadcbd2@role-real-estate-title.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260811T133935Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260811
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Title 5 License Maintenance Case
DESCRIPTION:Maine.gov\nAgencies\n|\nOnline Services\n|\nHelp\n|\nSearch Ma
 ine.gov\nDHHS\n→\nOffice of MaineCare Services (OMS)\n→\nProvider Reso
 urces\n→\n	 \n			Title 5 License Maintenance Case\nTitle 5 License Maint
 enance Case\nAug 11\, 2026\nProviders whose license is under a Title 5 rev
 iew may use your Title 5 notice to extend your enrollment with MaineCare i
 n MIHMS by six months\, and for every six months thereafter\, until the Ti
 tle 5 review is resolved. Providers must complete this update by submittin
 g a maintenance case via the Health PAS Online Portal. They can use the\nP
 rovider Maintenance User Guide\nfor step-by-step instructions.\nSelect the
  “Title 5 License Extension” from the licensing board drop-down menu a
 nd complete the maintenance case as usual. Providers can use the\nALMS web
 site\nto search for your license and must take a screenshot to upload with
  the maintenance case to show the Title 5 status.\nPlease ensure the "Term
  Date” is 6 months after the license expiration date. For example\, if y
 ou submit your Title 5 review and your license ends on January 30\, 2026\,
  extend the “Term Date” out to July 30\, 2026. As necessary\, repeat t
 his process every six months until the license is renewed. Once the licens
 e is renewed\, submit another case with the new term date of the license.\
 nProviders take note of your license expiration dates and plan to submit a
  maintenance case to update that license information a minimum of 30 days 
 prior to the license expiration date. Be sure to account for this when pl
 anning and submitting other maintenance cases.\nNote:\nMaineCare will\nnot
  reimburse providers\nfor services rendered when they fail to renew and up
 date your license within a maintenance case prior to its expiration.\nFor 
 questions about this process\, please contact Provider Enrollment at 1 (86
 6) 690-5585 option 2.\nhttps://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-b
 ulletins/title-5-license-maintenance-case-2026-08-11
URL:https://www.maine.gov/dhhs/oms/providers/provider-bulletins/title-5-li
 cense-maintenance-case-2026-08-11
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
